---
export const prerender = true;
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import FounderPhoto from '../components/FounderPhoto.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Card from '../components/Card.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';

const CONTACT_EMAIL = SITE.email;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Work with me — TomProtects"
  description="Fractional CISO and security advisory for growing businesses. What the work is, who it fits, and how to start a conversation."
>
  <Section width="text">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Work with me</h1>

    <div class="mt-8 max-w-2xl space-y-6 text-ink/70">
      <p>
        Fractional CISO and security advisory for growing businesses: helping you build your first
        real security program, and keeping it moving once it exists.
      </p>

      <p>
        Engagements vary, but they draw on the same
        <a href="/#how-i-help" class="font-medium text-accent underline underline-offset-4"
          >four areas</a
        >: understanding where you stand, knowing what to do next, keeping it moving, and handling
        newer risks calmly. Some businesses want one assessment and a roadmap they can run
        themselves. Others want someone in the room month to month. Both are reasonable places to
        start.
      </p>
    </div>

    <Callout on="cream" class="mt-8 max-w-2xl">
      <p class="text-ink/80">
        The work is advisory. I do not sell products and I do not take over your systems.
        Implementation happens through the IT staff or provider you already have, who know your
        environment. My part is making sure the right things happen, in the right order.
      </p>
    </Callout>
  </Section>

  <Section background="white" width="text">
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Who it fits</h2>

    <div class="mt-6 max-w-2xl space-y-6 text-ink/70">
      <p>
        Growing businesses, roughly five to fifty people, that depend on technology for nearly
        everything they do, have nobody whose actual job is security, and have started fielding
        questions from customers, insurers or regulators that are difficult to answer.
      </p>

      <p>
        It is worth saying what does not fit, too. If you already have a security team, or what you
        need is a penetration test, or a certification against a deadline, this is not the right
        engagement — and I would rather tell you that in the first ten minutes than three weeks in.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section width="text">
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Starting a conversation</h2>

    <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-ink/70">
      A first call is about where your business stands today, what is already being asked of it, and
      whether an engagement would help. No obligation either way, and nothing to price until there
      is something specific worth pricing.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8 flex items-center gap-4">
      <FounderPhoto class="h-16 w-16 shrink-0" />
      <p class="text-sm text-ink/70">
        You'll be talking to me directly — Tom. CISSP, CISM, CDPSE and PMP, and more than twenty
        years in security.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ul class="mt-8 max-w-2xl space-y-3 text-ink/80">
      {/*
        Deliberately no duration here. The calendar below is booked as a
        30-minute slot, and the v1 copy this page replaced said 15–20, so the
        two contradicted each other on the same screen. Whichever is right, it
        belongs in TidyCal — stating it twice only means it can drift again.
      */}
      <li class="flex gap-3">
        <span class="mt-0.5 font-bold text-accent">✓</span> A short call, no pressure, no pitch
      </li>
      <li class="flex gap-3">
        <span class="mt-0.5 font-bold text-accent">✓</span> Plain-English answers to your security
        questions
      </li>
      <li class="flex gap-3">
        <span class="mt-0.5 font-bold text-accent">✓</span> A clear sense of whether an engagement
        would help, and what it would involve
      </li>
    </ul>

    <!-- TidyCal scheduling embed — unchanged: same account, same path, same markup. -->
    <Card radius="2xl" padding="xs" class="mt-10 sm:p-4">
      <div class="tidycal-embed" data-path="tomsmith/discovery"></div>
      <script is:inline src="https://asset-tidycal.b-cdn.net/js/embed.js" async></script>
      <noscript>
        <p class="p-4 text-ink/70">
          The booking calendar needs JavaScript. You can also book directly at
          <a href="https://tidycal.com/tomsmith/discovery" class="font-medium text-accent underline underline-offset-4">tidycal.com/tomsmith/discovery</a>.
        </p>
      </noscript>
    </Card>

    <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-sm text-ink/70">
      Would rather write than book a slot? Email
      <a
        href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}
        class="font-medium text-accent underline underline-offset-4">{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a
      > and tell me where things stand.
    </p>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
